    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "pid": "p004",
      "raw_text": "一天早上五点多，方学东在门边对太太大叫：“不好了，起火了！”",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "sid": "s011",
          "text": "一天早上五点多，方学东在门边对太太大叫：“不好了，起火了！",
          "translation": "One morning at around five o'clock, Fang Xuedong shouted to his wife at the door, 'Oh no, there's a fire!'",
          "explanation": "This sentence introduces a common structure in Chinese where the time phrase comes before the subject. The use of '对' here indicates speaking directly to someone, and '大叫' is a verb meaning 'to shout loudly.'",
          "words": [
            {
              "hanzi": "一天",
              "pinyin": "yī tiān",
              "definition": "one day"
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "早上",
              "pinyin": "zǎo shàng",
              "definition": "morning"
            },
            {
