    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "pid": "p005",
      "raw_text": "“我的天！”方太太走出来，看到门边的东西起火了，马上又走进去。“我去拿水！”",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "sid": "s013",
          "text": "“我的天！",
          "translation": "My Heavens!",
          "explanation": "The phrase '我的天' is a common exclamation in Chinese, similar to saying 'Oh my goodness!' in English.",
          "words": [
            {
              "hanzi": "“",
              "pinyin": "“",
              "definition": "character"
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "我的",
              "pinyin": "wǒ de",
              "definition": "my"
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "天",
              "pinyin": "tiān",
              "definition": "heavens"
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "！",
              "pinyin": "",
              "definition": "exclamation mark"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "s014",
          "text": "”方太太走出来，看到门边的东西起火了，马上又走进去。",
          "translation": "Mrs. Fang came out and saw that something by the door was on fire, so she immediately went back inside.",
          "explanation": "The structure '看到...起火了' means 'saw that something was on fire', where '起火了' indicates that something caught on fire.",
          "words": [
            {
              "hanzi": "”",
              "pinyin": "”",
              "definition": "quotation mark (opening)"
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "方太太",
              "pinyin": "fāng tài tài",
              "definition": "Mrs. Fang"
